  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7265114aa1e7f41ada19d74a427f9e13, type: 3}
  m_Name: StressZeroGCCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: xpTURN.Feedback.Samples::xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.SampleCard
  Title: Stress & Zero-GC
  Try: Pick a player count and watch the meter; switch re-trigger on (every cube
    plays again once a second), then the coroutine baseline on and off.
  See: "The players are copies of one template (a cube with one long punch on itself
    \u2014 the package's performance test's shape), built 500 a frame, each played
    once, and destroyed when the count drops: that steady state is the test's. Re-trigger
    adds a start and a stop per cube a second. The meter's allocation is the frame's
    against the baseline taken when the comparison was last switched: the players
    stay at it, the coroutine baseline (a coroutine and a delay object per start)
    climbs while re-triggered. The three Feedback markers and the main thread are
    the profiler's \u2014 a development build reads them exactly, the editor adds
    its own work, a release build has none. Don't select the cubes in the Hierarchy
    while measuring (the inspector rebuilds what it shows). The players are made
    at run time \u2014 the HUD's Select Player does not pick them."
  Controls: "Z \xB7 X \xB7 C \xB7 V \xB7 D-pad \u2014 player count \xB7 2 \xB7 Gamepad
    West \u2014 coroutine baseline \xB7 3 \xB7 Gamepad North \u2014 re-trigger \xB7
    Mouse \u2014 buttons"
  SceneGuid: 2e6e67bd9e96243c0af68ba875d271aa
  SceneName: StressZeroGC
  RequiredType: xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.Advanced.StressLab, xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.Advanced.StressZeroGC
  RequiresText: 
  OpenInEditor: 0
